11
00:31:51,724 --> 00:31:57,724
Flushed Away is a 2006 animated adventure comedy film produced by
DreamWorks Animation SKG and Aardman Features.

12
00:34:45,517 --> 00:34:51,517
The film was directed by David Bowers and Sam Fell, and written by Dick
Clement, Ian La Frenais, Chris Lloyd, Joe Keenan and Will Davies.

13
00:37:39,310 --> 00:37:45,310
The film stars the voices of Hugh Jackman, Kate Winslet, Ian McKellen,
Shane Richie, Bill Nighy, Andy Serkis and Jean Reno.

14
00:40:33,103 --> 00:40:39,103
In the film, a fancy rat named Roddy St.

15
00:43:26,896 --> 00:43:32,896
James is flushed down the toilet in his Kensington apartment and befriends a scavenger
named Rita Malone in order to get back home while evading a sinister toad.

16
00:46:20,689 --> 00:46:26,689
Flushed Away was the third and final DreamWorks and Aardman co-production following
Chicken Run (2000) and Wallace & Gromit: The Curse of the Were-Rabbit (2005).

17
00:49:14,482 --> 00:49:20,482
Director Fell conceived the concept of rats falling in love
in the sewers while working on Chicken Run.

18
00:52:08,275 --> 00:52:14,275
In 2001, Fell developed a story and pitched it to DreamWorks.

19
00:55:02,068 --> 00:55:08,068
The project was announced in July 2002, followed by comedy writing duo Clement and La Frenais
being contracted to write the script, which had the working title Ratropolis.

20
00:57:55,862 --> 00:58:01,862
In 2003, Bowers joined Fell as co-director.

21
01:00:49,655 --> 01:00:55,655
It was the first Aardman project made primarily in CGI animation instead of using their usual
claymation – this was because using water on plasticine models could damage them.

22
01:03:43,448 --> 01:03:49,448
The film's premiere was held on 22 October 2006 during the Tokyo International Film Festival, followed by a wide release in
the United States by Paramount Pictures on 3 November 2006, and in the United Kingdom by UIP on 1 December.

23
01:06:37,241 --> 01:06:43,241
It received positive reviews from critics, but was a box-office disappointment, grossing $178 million against a
$149 million production budget, resulting in an estimated loss of $109 million for the studios.

24
01:09:31,034 --> 01:09:37,034
The failure led to Aardman ending its collaboration deal with DreamWorks.

25
01:12:24,827 --> 01:12:30,827
The film received nominations for the BAFTA Award and
Critics' Choice Award for Best Animated Feature.

26
01:15:18,620 --> 01:15:24,620
It received eight nominations at the 34th Annie Awards, winning five,
including for the screenplay and, for McKellen, Voice Acting.

27
01:18:12,413 --> 01:18:18,413
The film explores themes of ship, london, england, return, villain, girlfriend.

28
01:21:06,206 --> 01:21:12,206
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
